Let ${\mathsf{A_n^k}}$ denote the set of $k$-arrangements of size $n$. For a $k$-arrangement represented by a permutation $\pi$, color each fixed point using a map from ${\mathsf{Fix}}(\pi)$ to $[k]$, and assign color $0$ elsewhere; this produces its **color-encoding** $(\pi,c)$. Let $\mathop{{\sf inv}}
olimits$, $\mathop{{\sf maj}}
olimits$, and $\mathop{\sf des}
olimits$ be the corresponding statistics on colored permutations. **Color-encoding equidistribution conjecture.** The statistics $\mathop{{\sf inv}}
olimits$ and $\mathop{{\sf maj}}
olimits$ are equidistributed on ${\mathsf{A_n^k}}$ in the color encoding for any $n$ and $k$. Moreover, $\mathop{\sf des}
olimits$ in the color encoding has the same distribution on ${\mathsf{A_n^k}}$ as $\mathop{\sf des}
olimits$ in the permutation or derangement form, for any $n$ and $k$. The parser supplies no resolution evidence, so this conjecture remains open in this record.
